# WHAT IT COVERS: the 2026-10-27 stream, 17.5 minutes cut to the gameplay its video shows,
# captured through Windows.Graphics.Capture with o:vsync: a synthesized present is drawn by the
# optical flow warp, or by the blend when the flow was planned too late or not at all. That
# changes how a synthesized present looks and nothing the replay models; the policy is the one
# the tree ships. The first o:vsync stream through Windows.Graphics.Capture here. The game
# hitched (20 to 100 ms) 104 times (356 an hour) and stalled for 100 ms or more 18 times (62 an
# hour), in 35 bursts, 11 of them with a stall, and with no periodic stretch. The lock released
# 12 times, 41 an hour, at 542.39, 906.69, 917.26, 987.14 s and then 8 times in 13 s, 1084.58 to
# 1097.51 s, where the game hitched 16 times in 16.5 s (1080.9 s to 1097.4 s, up to 26 ms, no
# stall) on the walk out of a barn. The worst blend run, 38 presents in the field and on the
# dejitter arm, sits in that stretch at 1086.73 s. Of the 33 moves on the replay, 6 of them
# late, 8 land more than 2 ms from a real frame.
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 50.594 s, from the 2397
# marked frames in its first 39 s, all on time within 0.36 ms of that offset (p90). The video
# runs 1050.4 s with no holes, opens on gameplay at a table in town (marked) and ends on
# gameplay leaving the barn, after a minute of the game's read and sleep wheels, which kept the
# gameplay frame rate. The cut is the whole video, 50.6 s to 1101.0 s of log time, and the marked
# frames lie inside it. Inside the cut, 6 seconds in 6 runs fall out of the 60 fps regime, each a
# single hitch second.
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay line reads synth 1.2% against 1.1%, worst run 39 against 38, runs >= 50 0 against 0 and
# pull wraps 25 against 23. On the dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran, blends are 702
# against 704, repeats 160 against 160, skips 57 against 57, pull wraps 79.1 an hour against
# 78.8 and the worst run 38 against 38. The replay makes 33 moves and the field's log has 33 in
# the window; all 12 field releases match the replay's within 0.49 ms, with none on one side
# only.
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
